  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43788522",
      "title": "Using Getters For Computed Values",
      "lectureOrder": 25,
      "videoOrder": 21,
      "sourceHash": "2402cd668c86f070aaabc90693fba7f5a78eff72801fdcc119718e4de2fbb4ba",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.64,
          "en": "So you did now learn",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.64,
          "end": 6.39,
          "en": "how you can output dynamic data in your templates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.39,
          "end": 10.113,
          "en": "with help of string interpolation and property binding.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.25,
          "end": 15.48,
          "en": "Now, you will fairly often have cases like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.48,
          "end": 18.99,
          "en": "where you might need to compute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.99,
          "end": 20.85,
          "en": "a value that should be output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.85,
          "end": 23.37,
          "en": "So where you maybe need to construct a value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.37,
          "end": 28.14,
          "en": "like this string here, which consists of multiple values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.14,
          "end": 31.56,
          "en": "in this case, the avatar property of the selected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.56,
          "end": 34.89,
          "en": "user object and this fixed string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.89,
          "end": 38.7,
          "en": "And as you can of course, see, you can do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.7,
          "end": 40.923,
          "en": "directly inside of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.79,
          "end": 45.36,
          "en": "However, it is considered a better practice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 45.36,
          "end": 49.74,
          "en": "to keep your template code, the dynamic template code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 49.74,
          "end": 54.57,
          "en": "fairly simple and to outsource computations like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.57,
          "end": 56.49,
          "en": "into a different place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 56.49,
          "end": 59.88,
          "en": "That's why I will cut this dynamic value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.88,
          "end": 63.03,
          "en": "from the user component HTML file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 63.03,
          "end": 65.52,
          "en": "And instead I'll use another TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 65.52,
          "end": 70.17,
          "en": "and JavaScript feature that you can use in classes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 70.17,
          "end": 73.05,
          "en": "I'll add a so-called getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.05,
          "end": 77.31,
          "en": "By adding the get keyword and then any identifier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.31,
          "end": 81.3,
          "en": "of your choice, for example, imagePath,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 81.3,
          "end": 83.193,
          "en": "though that name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.24,
          "end": 87.48,
          "en": "Then you add opening and closing parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.48,
          "end": 90.213,
          "en": "and then opening and closing curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 91.32,
          "end": 94.68,
          "en": "And this creates a so-called getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.68,
          "end": 99.68,
          "en": "It's essentially a method, so a function inside of a class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 99.99000000000001,
          "end": 104.61,
          "en": "that's usable like a property so that does not need",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.61,
          "end": 108.45,
          "en": "to be called and executed explicitly, and that's meant",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 108.45,
          "end": 111.66,
          "en": "to produce and return a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 111.66,
          "end": 115.47,
          "en": "And the new value that should be produced and returned here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 117.963,
          "en": "is that path to the image.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 123.78,
          "en": "Now here I'm now referring to that selected user property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 123.78,
          "end": 127.38,
          "en": "And since I'm now doing this from inside the class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 127.38,
          "end": 131.94,
          "en": "instead of from inside the template, as we did it before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 131.94,
          "end": 136.94,
          "en": "we must add the this keyword and a dot in front of that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 137.04,
          "end": 140.22,
          "en": "Because that's how in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 140.22,
          "end": 144.54,
          "en": "it's not TypeScript specific, but in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 144.54,
          "end": 147.84,
          "en": "how you access properties of a class",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 147.84,
          "end": 150.66,
          "en": "from within that same class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 154.05,
          "en": "So with the this keyword, we access this class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 154.05,
          "end": 156.66,
          "en": "so to say, to which this getter belongs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 156.66,
          "end": 160.5,
          "en": "and we can then get hold of the different other properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 160.5,
          "end": 162.99,
          "en": "that may be defined in that class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 162.99,
          "end": 165.423,
          "en": "like this selected user property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 166.35,
          "end": 169.14,
          "en": "And with that, we now got this image path getter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 169.14,
          "end": 171.81,
          "en": "and you can now use that getter just like",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 171.81,
          "end": 174.87,
          "en": "any other property in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 174.87,
          "end": 178.53,
          "en": "So here as a value for the source property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 178.53,
          "end": 182.283,
          "en": "we can now use this image path like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 183.12,
          "end": 185.79,
          "en": "As I mentioned, like a property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 185.79,
          "end": 189.51,
          "en": "So you don't execute it. You don't add parentheses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 189.51,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "Even though it's defined like a method here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "But because it's such a getter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "because of that get keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 199.683,
          "en": "you use it like a property, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 204.66,
          "en": "And with that, you'll get the same result as before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 204.66,
          "end": 207.543,
          "en": "But now the template is written in a cleaner way.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
